The Rolls
Posted byPieceOfPrincessDecember 26, 2020Posted inSims
Now the fun begins! Time to get to rolling the dice! There are in total 5 main rolls to make:
Marital Status – Number of Children – Careers – Generation Goals – Miscellaneous Fun

A) Marital Status
Set the Dice 1 – 54
[1-10] Single Parent: Raise the kids by yourself
[10-30] Couple: Live together with a romantic interest and use the help to raise the kids.
[31-32] Mixed Single: Have both adopted and biological children. Must have at least 2 children.
[33-34] Mixed Couple: Same as #17 but with the romantic interest.
[35-36] Second Chance: Have a child with the first partner, but get another partner after.
[37-38] Single with Help: Another sim lives with you, who is not romantically involved.
[39] Mixed Single with Help: Combine the variations above.
[40] Couple with Help
[41] Mixed Couple with Help
[42] Single with double Help
[43] Mixed Single with double Help
[44] Full house: 3 extra sims that can help raise kids (4 sims including the heir in total in any relations as you’d like)
[45] Single with “useless” help: Raise the kids by yourself, but you’re getting an extra hand around: you should have a butler, gardener (if you have a garden), a nanny (if you have kids aged child and younger), etc. All roles should help out! Get your wallet ready. However, you cannot instruct them on or push them to do certain tasks.
[46] Couple with “useless” help: Same as #26 but as a couple.
[47] Full Occult House: 3 extra Occult sims that can help raise kids (4 sims including the heir in total in any relations as you’d like).
[48] Full Pet House: Single with 3 additional pets (preferably one dog, one cat and one horse. But it can be any combination). Re-roll if you don’t have any pets.
[49] Black Widow: Second-Chance style, but somehow your heir seems to be cursed. Your sim must marry at least 3 times and all previous partners must have died in mysterious ways. Must have a child with the first partner. If you roll more than one kid, you can decide within which marriage the children come from.
[50] Multi-family dwelling: You must move to a Residential Rental lot together with your remaining family members. However, they should have their own rental place to stay while you build your current generations family. Re-roll to decide what kind of marital status this generation will have while your parent(s)/siblings/other people you grew up with will still be around in the background. If applicable, also move your spouses’ family into the Residential Rental lot to also keep them around.
[51-52] Second chance (again..): You must have each child with another partner. They must live with you until you find another suitable partner until you settled down. Re-roll if you rolled for 1 or two kids.
[53] Multiplied Love (LS): Love is in the air as a polyamorous sim with 2 partners. Re-roll if preferred to play in other dynamics.
[54] Shared Custody: Have a partner, get pregnant/adopt/have a science baby immediatly (if you rolled for more than 1 child, have them back-to-back). After the last rolled kid is born, split up and decide custody via a roll. Whoever spends more time with the kid has primary custody and gets Child Support.
Child Support Steps:
Roll 1–7 to determine how many days per week the child stays with the other parent. (If using AA, this can be done via a Getaway instead.)
#1 Primary Custody – 1 day per week with Ex
#2 Primary Custody – 2 days per week with Ex
#3 Primary Custody – 3 days per week with Ex
#4 Equal Custody – 4 days with each parent
#5 Secondary Custody – 3 days per week with Heir
#6 Secondary Custody – 2 days per week with Heir
#7 Secondary Custody – 1 day per week with Heir

B) Number of Children
Set the Dice 1 – 10
[1-2] 1 Kid
[3-6] 2 Kids
[7-8] 3 Kids
[9] 4 Kids
[10] 5 Kids

